WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.220
In terms of major paychecks for movie stars,
the MCU got off to a relatively modest start.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:10.020
Since then, though, thanks to sequel contracts,
bonuses, and gross percentages, many of the

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:14.420
MCU's stars have made serious bank, and some
of them have joined the ranks of the highest-paid

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:15.340
actors in the world.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.960
Here's a look at some of the reported top
earners.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:22.760
Marvel Studios has historically done its best
to save on upfront costs of production by

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:27.340
paying its new stars a relatively small sum
for starring in superhero films, then offering

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:32.410
more significant pay in the form of backend
compensation like bonuses and box office percentages.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:37.510
This is how Robert Downey Jr. went from earning
six figures for Iron Man in 2008 to taking

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:42.080
home $75 million for Avengers: Infinity War
in 2018.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:45.719
Still, even Marvel's upfront earnings for
its stars have grown along with the studio's

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:49.489
box office success, and that shows when it
comes to stars like Chadwick Boseman.

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:54.260
Boseman, who debuted as Black Panther in 2016's
Captain America: Civil War, got his first

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:56.369
solo superhero film in 2018.

00:00:56.369 --> 00:01:00.519
Black Panther was a worldwide phenomenon and
currently reigns as the tenth highest-grossing

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:05.020
film of all time, making it Marvel's most
successful solo superhero movie effort.

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:09.080
Boseman was reportedly paid $2 million to
star in the film, which is an impressive number

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:10.760
for his first Marvel solo movie.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.500
Compared to what the film ultimately earned,
though, it feels like Marvel got a bargain.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:20.040
Brie Larson's 2019 debut in the Marvel Cinematic
Universe had a lot riding on it, and not just

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:24.200
because it was an attempt to introduce yet
another sub-franchise into the Marvel Studios

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:24.700
family.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:29.479
Captain Marvel, starring Larson in the title
role, was the studio's first female-led superhero

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:29.980
film.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:33.900
Fans hoped it would be another breakthrough
film for diversity in the genre, much like

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.820
Black Panther was in early 2018.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:42.060
The film ultimately took in $1.12 billion
worldwide, and Larson is set to be a major

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.180
piece of Marvel's storytelling going forward.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:45.280
The effort paid off.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:49.159
Even before we all knew what Captain Marvel
would be, though, Larson — who was already

00:01:49.159 --> 00:01:53.079
an Oscar winner for her role in Room when
she was cast in the MCU — was looking for

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:56.759
a payday that was going to give her a solid
foundation, particularly when it came to pay

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:58.520
equity with male co-stars.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:04.140
To that end, her ultimate Captain Marvel payday
was reportedly $5 million, or ten times what

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:08.180
Robert Downey Jr. made upfront to star in
Iron Man back in 2008.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:15.340
Samuel L. Jackson's filmography is the highest-grossing
of any actor on the planet, at more than $13.3

00:02:15.349 --> 00:02:20.360
billion worldwide, thanks in no small part
to his ability to become a part of major franchises

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:21.820
even if he's not in a leading role.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.060
This happened with the Star Wars prequels,
and it's happened again with the MCU, in which

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:29.740
he's been appearing ever since the post-credits
scene of Iron Man back in 2008.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:30.940
"Who the hell are you?"

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.500
"Nick Fury, director of S.H.I.E.L.D."

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:36.240
"Oh."

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.340
"I'm here to talk to you about the Avenger
initiative."

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:44.360
2019 alone finds Jackson appearing in three
different Marvel films, though his roles in

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:46.260
the films range from sidekick to cameo.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:50.480
That makes his overall salary for the flicks
very hard to pin down, but Jackson's certainly

00:02:50.489 --> 00:02:53.580
made an effort to keep on par with some of
the franchise's bigger stars.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:58.709
For The Avengers in 2012, he reportedly took
home somewhere between $4-6 million after

00:02:58.709 --> 00:03:03.030
bonuses came in, and for Avengers: Age of
Ultron he was among the cast members who reportedly

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:07.660
went after at least $5 million upfront, plus
even more once the film started to make serious

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:08.160
money.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:12.560
There's no word on his Spider-Man: Far From
Home payday just yet, but Jackson has said

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:16.430
he'd happily keep playing Nick Fury for as
long as Marvel will have him, so there's a

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:17.840
lot of earning potential left there.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:21.620
Before Mark Ruffalo was in the picture, Edward
Norton played the Hulk.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:25.599
Norton ultimately bowed out of the MCU due
to various creative differences.

00:03:25.599 --> 00:03:29.920
So, when it came time to make The Avengers,
Ruffalo was the only member of the main team

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:33.280
who hadn't already appeared in some capacity
in another MCU flick.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:37.580
"Should have got paid up front, Banner."

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:42.219
That could have put him at a disadvantage,
but he mostly kept pace with his co-stars.

00:03:42.219 --> 00:03:46.069
Ruffalo reportedly joined the club of actors
— including Chris Hemsworth, Chris Evans,

00:03:46.069 --> 00:03:50.880
and Jeremy Renner — who managed to earn
$2 to $3 million for The Avengers after bonuses,

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:55.250
and then also became one of the team members
who pushed for a raise to the $5 million range

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:56.880
for Avengers: Age of Ultron.

00:03:57.129 --> 00:04:01.200
There's no reliable reporting on what came
next for him in terms of pay for Thor: Ragnarok

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:05.390
and the last two Avengers movies, but Ruffalo
likely got his due for continuing his wonderful

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:06.980
work as Dr. Bruce Banner.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:11.980
Benedict Cumberbatch was already a pop culture
fan-favorite and award winner before he was

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:14.750
tapped to play surgeon-turned-sorcerer Doctor
Strange.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:16.540
A bigger name means a bigger paycheck.

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:18.780
Did the MCU money guys deliver?

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:19.620
You bet.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:24.320
For his MCU debut in 2016's Doctor Strange,
Cumberbatch reportedly earned a little more

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:25.780
than $3 million.

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:29.920
That solo film, plus his cameo appearance
in Thor: Ragnarok and his supporting roles

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:34.880
in Avengers: Infinity War and Avengers: Endgame,
bumped his Marvel payday up to about $5 million

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:36.220
by 2019.

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:41.020
Cumberbatch's success in the MCU so far is
about to lead to even bigger things.

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:45.540
According to The Mirror, the actor is negotiating
for a nearly $10 million payday for the upcoming

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:46.760
Doctor Strange sequel.

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:51.180
"Dormammu…

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:52.880
I've come to bargain."

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:55.780
"You've come to die."

00:04:55.940 --> 00:05:00.300
Like the other major "Phase One" MCU stars,
Chris Hemsworth had to settle for a relatively

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:04.560
low payday at first, but as the films grew
in popularity, his initial pay and the bonuses

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.340
he stood to earn continued to climb.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:10.910
Though his Thor paycheck was relatively small,
Hemsworth's pay swelled by the time of the

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:15.400
first Avengers film, earning him $2-3 million
with various box office bonuses.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:18.580
As the sequels piled up, so too did the higher
paychecks.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:23.580
That deal reportedly shot up to $5 million
upfront plus future bonuses for Avengers:

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:28.060
Age of Ultron, and, by the time the "Infinity
Saga" neared its Endgame, Hemsworth's payout

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.060
had swelled even more.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:33.880
Sources say he collected something in the
range of $15 to $20 million for Thor: Ragnarok,

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:36.950
and took home similar paychecks for both Infinity
War and Endgame.

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:40.710
Plus, the finale of Endgame leaves plenty
of room for Hemsworth to keep earning Marvel

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:42.140
money in future films.

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:46.300
There's a remarkable degree of symmetry to
the Marvel careers of Chris Evans and Chris

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:49.550
Hemsworth, at least when it comes to the rise
of their respective salaries.

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:53.630
Evans, like Hemsworth, arrived with a relatively
low payday for Captain America: The First

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:57.240
Avenger, but things started to really pick
up when it came time to finally assemble the

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:58.340
team with The Avengers.

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:02.900
Like Hemsworth, Evans reportedly earned a
final paycheck in the $2-3 million range for

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:05.880
that film, and then started aiming even higher
for sequels.

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:10.740
Evans was also among the group of actors who
angled for a $5 million upfront paycheck for

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:13.640
Avengers: Age of Ultron, and then came Captain
America: Civil War.

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:18.620
Evans reportedly renegotiated a payday of
$15 million for that film, and by the time

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:22.930
the last two Avengers flicks rolled around,
Evans was, like Hemsworth, also aiming for

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:25.540
a payday in the $15-20 million range.

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:30.820
Scarlett Johansson is just now getting her
own Black Widow solo movie, despite being

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:32.960
one of the MCU's longest-serving stars.

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:37.200
She first appeared in a supporting role in
Iron Man 2, then transitioned into being the

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:40.920
first — and, for a little while, the only
— female member of the Avengers, making

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:43.960
her an integral part of the MCU throughout
the Infinity Saga.

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:48.890
Johansson was an established movie star before
the MCU kicked off, so even her earliest Marvel

00:06:48.890 --> 00:06:50.160
paydays were substantial.

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:54.860
She reportedly earned somewhere in the neighborhood
of $4-6 million for her work on The Avengers

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:57.680
after collecting various box office bonuses
on that film.

00:06:57.940 --> 00:07:01.380
Her numbers have climbed since then, but for
Johansson the best is yet to come.

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:06.640
Black Widow will net her a reported $20 million
payday for serving as both star and producer.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:12.180
When Iron Man arrived in 2008, Robert Downey
Jr. immediately hit a new level of stardom.

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:16.740
Downey's initial pay for Iron Man was rather
small compared to where he ended up, but bonuses

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:19.820
based on the film's box office gross helped
pad that number out.

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:23.900
Then, in the wake of the film's success, Downey
and his reps started renegotiating, and the

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:27.620
paychecks for the Godfather of the MCU just
kept gaining more zeroes.

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:28.680
"The truth is…

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:36.440
I am Iron Man."

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:41.480
Downey was ultimately able to cut a deal with
Marvel Studios by which he collects a hefty

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:46.460
backend earnings percentage not just from
Iron Man solo films, but from Avengers movies.

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:51.110
The actual percentage is not publicly known,
but it's reportedly in the 5-7 percent range,

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:52.710
which would mean massive earnings.

00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:56.020
According to The Hollywood Reporter, Downey
took home somewhere in the neighborhood of

00:07:56.020 --> 00:08:01.180
$75 million for Avengers: Infinity War, a
number that likely climbed for Avengers: Endgame.

